---
import Publication from "../layouts/Publication.astro";
import SourceLink from "../components/SourceLink.astro";
import Diagram from "../components/Diagram.astro";
import chapters from "../data/chapters.json";
import { base } from "../lib/registers.mjs";
---

<Publication
  title="Credit risk: the complete research record"
  summary="A technical dossier of the lending decision, model experiments, evidence, serving design and unfinished work."
  headings={[
    { id: "decision", label: "Start with the lending decision" },
    { id: "read", label: "Read the record" },
    { id: "audit", label: "Audit the evidence" },
  ]}
>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2 id="decision">
      Start with the lending decision<a
        class="header-anchor"
        href="#decision"
        aria-label="Link to lending decision">#</a
      >
    </h2><p>
      A lender needs to estimate loan risk before committing principal. The
      project predicts the probability of charge-off from a borrower profile,
      then uses measured loss severity and assumed costs to illustrate price.
    </p><p>
      This publication explains why each decision was made, how it was
      implemented, what its evidence supports and what would invalidate it. It
      uses the <SourceLink id="notebook" label="research notebook" />, <SourceLink
        id="defense"
        label="defense guide"
      /> and <SourceLink id="evidence-dir" label="recorded evidence" /> as sources.
    </p>
  </section>
  <aside class="callout limitation">
    <strong>The serving gap is central</strong><p>
      Full-feature notebook performance does not validate the browser form. That
      form defaults 40 model inputs. XGBoost’s small gain over logistic
      regression is also inconclusive, and the price rule remains illustrative.
    </p><a href={base + "chapters/training-serving/"}
      >Read training versus serving →</a
    >
  </aside>
  <Diagram id="business" />
  <section>
    <h2 id="read">
      Read the record<a
        class="header-anchor"
        href="#read"
        aria-label="Link to chapter list">#</a
      >
    </h2><ol class="chapter-index">
      {
        chapters.map((c) => (
          <li>
            <a href={base + "chapters/" + c.slug + "/"}>
              <>
                <span class="chapter-number">
                  {String(c.number).padStart(2, "0")}
                </span>
                <span>
                  <>
                    <strong>{c.title}</strong>
                    <small>{c.summary}</small>
                  </>
                </span>
              </>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </section>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2 id="audit">
      Audit the evidence<a
        class="header-anchor"
        href="#audit"
        aria-label="Link to evidence tools">#</a
      >
    </h2><p>
      Use the <a href={base + "evidence/"}>evidence register</a>, <a
        href={base + "fields/"}>field audit</a
      >, <a href={base + "timeline/"}>decision ledger</a>, <a
        href={base + "limitations/"}>limitations register</a
      > and <a href={base + "sources/"}>source map</a>. Recorded reproduction
      and saved notebook output have distinct labels.
    </p><p>
      The complete text and registers are static HTML. JavaScript adds local
      search, filters and copy controls. This site needs no model server.
    </p>
  </section>
</Publication>
